  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Conics in standard and general form, transformations, and polar coordinates are tested on advanced ACT and ACT subject items.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Parabola (vertical)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (x-h)^2=4p(y-k) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Ellipse",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Hyperbola",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Polar",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( x=r\\cos\\theta,\\ y=r\\sin\\theta \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Convert the polar point \\( \\left(4,\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right) \\) to Cartesian. \\[ x=4\\cos\\tfrac{\\pi}{3}=4\\cdot\\tfrac{1}{2}=2,\\quad y=4\\sin\\tfrac{\\pi}{3}=4\\cdot\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}=2\\sqrt3. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Conics in Standard Form & 3D Distance",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Completing the square converts a general conic to standard form. <strong>3D distance:</strong> \\(d = \\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2+(z_2-z_1)^2}\\). A <strong>rotation</strong> of axes by \\(\\theta\\) transforms \\(x = X\\cos\\theta - Y\\sin\\theta\\), \\(y = X\\sin\\theta + Y\\cos\\theta\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Complete the square to find a circle",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Write \\(x^2+y^2-6x+4y-3=0\\) in standard form. <p>\\((x^2-6x+9)+(y^2+4y+4) = 3+9+4 = 16\\). Centre \\((3,-2)\\), radius \\(4\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find the distance between points \\(A(1,2,3)\\) and \\(B(4,6,3)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(d = \\sqrt{(4-1)^2+(6-2)^2+(3-3)^2} = \\sqrt{9+16+0} = \\sqrt{25} = 5\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
